      "source_test": "test_an_internal_notice_only_turn_does_not_create_a_recursive_notice",
      "coverage": "A real Ticket failure creates a real Manager wake/batch. The existing connected/bind fixture links a Chief-held Ticket to the idle Manager recipient, mirroring the source linked-Ticket arrangement; this is not a claim that normal owner routes create this association. Real batch delivery is the only prompt in the tested turn. Failure must create no recursive wake for the linked Ticket."
    },
    {
      "source_test": "test_a_sender_cannot_spoof_notice_suppression_with_the_internal_prefix",
      "coverage": "An ordinary owner prompt reuses the exact sender ID captured from the genuine batch delivered to another conversation. Its failed turn must create one Chief-targeted wake, proving durable conversation membership rather than prefix spelling controls suppression."
    }
